## Requirements

- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (installs Python 3.14 and everything else)
{%- if is_django %}
- Node 24+ with [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) (`corepack enable`)
- Docker, for the local Postgres
{%- endif %}

## Getting started

```sh
uv run just setup     # dependencies and git hooks
{%- if is_django %}
uv run just up        # start Postgres
uv run just migrate
uv run just dev       # Django on :8000, Vite on :5173
{%- elif is_cli %}
uv run {{ project_slug }} hello Ada
{%- endif %}
uv run just check     # everything CI runs
```

`just` is installed into the project environment. Install it globally (or
activate `.venv`) to drop the `uv run` prefix. `just` on its own lists every recipe.

## Layout

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
{%- if is_django %}
  interface/     api/ and ui/ entry points
{%- elif is_cli %}
  interface/     the command line
{%- endif %}
  usecases/      orchestration; the only caller of vendors
  domain/        business rules
  vendors/       external systems
  data/          {% if is_django %}models and queries{% else %}persistence and data structures{% endif %}
  utils/         generic helpers
{%- if is_django %}
  settings/      base, dev, test, prod
frontend/src/    TypeScript and {% if is_tailwind %}Tailwind{% else %}Bootstrap{% endif %}, built by Vite
{%- endif %}
tests/           unit, integration, functional
```

Each layer is organised by feature. Layering is enforced by Import Linter. See [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the
rules and conventions.

## Configuration

{% if is_library -%}
The library reads no configuration from the environment.
{%- else -%}
Environment variables are declared and validated in
